prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 41 of them, the most of any pair. In 2025 that same middle ran 150% of normal in April to May and 47% in October to November. So far in 2026 it shows 36% of normal in March to April. July to August is the wettest pair at 8.66 inches of normal, and January to February is the driest at 5.96.</p>"}
